+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+The rental desk can only learn whether an item is free by trying to book it. Staff need to see at a glance
+which boards and sails can still be rented for a given period.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `availability(query)` to the rental service, with `query` = `{ start, end, kind? }`.
+- It returns the sorted ids of the equipment of that kind (any kind when `kind` is omitted) that is free for
+  the whole period, using the same whole-day UTC period rules and overlap rule as `book`.
+
+In scope: the read-only `availability` operation, its validation, and tests.
+Out of scope: cancellation, season (April to October) enforcement, customers and lessons, persistence,
+returning prices or booking details, and any change to `quote` or `book` behavior.
+
+No runtime dependency is introduced.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `equipment-rental`: adds an availability requirement (rentals at the booking desk).
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts`: `RentalService` interface and `createRentalService`.
+- `test/rental.test.ts`: new tests.
+- Existing behavior of `addEquipment`, `quote` and `book` is unchanged.
